<title>UK: ABF reaches record high on short squeeze.</title>
<headline>ABF reaches record high on short squeeze.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A short squeeze in Associated British Foods Plc powered the stock to a new high on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1114 GMT the stock was up 18p, or 4.1 percent, at a new high of 458-1/2p. The stock spiked to its previous high of 455p on December 3.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a big squeeze going on, people are short of the stock,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>&quot;It's similar to what happened with Burmah yesterday. There are just no sellers around in ABF today.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
